#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4134
msgid ""
"The slices by default are plotted clockwise starting from the vertical which"
" is considered 0 degrees. The first option allows the user to set a "
"different starting point for the pie series by changing the value in the "
"spin box. The value will increase to 360 degrees and then reset to zero."
msgstr ""
"Sektorerna ritas som standard medurs från lodräta riktningen, som motsvarar "
"0 grader. Med det första alternativet anger du en annan startpunkt för "
"cirkeldiagrammets serie i sifferfältet. Värdet ökar till 360 grader och "
"återgår sedan till noll."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4167
msgid "Bar and Column plots"
msgstr "Stapeldiagram och kolumndiagram"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4169
msgid ""
"Bar and column plots can be displayed with different sized gaps between "
"categories and different overlaps between the values of different series in "
"each category."
msgstr ""
"Du kan ändra mellanrummet mellan kategorier och överlappningen mellan olika "
"dataseriers värden i stapeldiagram och kolumndiagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4176
msgid "The configurable properties of bar and column plots."
msgstr "Egenskaper som kan ställas in för stapeldiagram och kolumndiagram."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4184
msgid ""
"This screenshot depicts the properties of bar and column plots which can be "
"configured."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar vilka egenskaper för stapeldiagram och kolumndiagram som "
"kan ställas in."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4193
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Gap</guilabel> describes the separation between the values "
"plotted in each category. By default, the gap between categories is one and "
"half times the width of a bar or a column. This spin button can be used to "
"decrease the gap to zero, so there is no gap between categories, or increase"
" the gap to 500% so the gap is five times the size of a bar or a column."
msgstr ""
"Värdet för <guilabel>Mellanrum</guilabel> anger avståndet mellan värdena i "
"varje kategori. Som standard är mellanrummet mellan kategorierna en och en "
"halv gång så stort som stapelns eller kolumnens bredd. Minska värdet till "
"noll om du vill ta bort mellanrummet, eller öka det till 500 %, då blir det "
"fem gånger så stort som stapeln eller kolumnen."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4203
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Overlap</guilabel> describes the separation between values of "
"the different series in each category. By default these values will be "
"plotted immediately adjacent to each other. This spin button can be lowered "
"to minus 100% which leaves a gap the size of a bar or column between the "
"values of each series. Alternatively, the values can be made to overlap up "
"to 100%, a complete overlap. When values completely overlap, the latter "
"series are plotted on top of the first series and a value may be completely "
"obscured. In this case it may be possible to use partially transparent "
"colors for the different series to allow both values to be visible."
msgstr ""
"Värdet för <guilabel>Överlappning</guilabel> anger avståndet mellan olika "
"dataseriers värden i varje kategori. Som standard ritas värdena intill "
"varandra. Med sifferfältet kan du minska överlappningen till −100 %, så att "
"det blir ett mellanrum stort som en stapel eller kolumn mellan värdena i "
"varje serie. Du kan också öka den till 100 %, så att värdena överlappar "
"helt. Då ritas senare serier ovanpå den första, som kan döljas helt. Använd "
"delvis genomskinliga färger för serierna om du vill se båda värdena."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4314
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Center size</guilabel> option determines the size of the hole "
"in the middle of the rings as a fraction of the total radius. The center "
"size can be altered in 5 percent increments."
msgstr ""
"Alternativet <guilabel>Hålets storlek</guilabel> anger hålets storlek i "
"förhållande till ringarnas totala radie. Du kan ändra storleken i steg om 5 "
"procent."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4321
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Vary colors by slice</guilabel> check box allows the user to "
"assign colors either by slices, which is the default, or by series. To use "
"color to distinguish series rather than categories, this button should not "
"be checked."
msgstr ""
"Med kryssrutan <guilabel>Variera färg mellan sektorer</guilabel> väljer du "
"om färger ska tilldelas per sektor, vilket är standard, eller per serie. "
"Avmarkera rutan om färgerna ska skilja serier åt i stället för kategorier."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4339
msgid "Data Series"
msgstr "Dataserier"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4341
msgid ""
"Each plot will have one or more 'series' which organize the data values. "
"Each series element has a number of properties. The element will have a "
"<guilabel>Style</guilabel> tab with which the style of the line and point "
"markers, or the area and outline can be set. Each series element will have a"
" <guilabel>Data</guilabel> tab in which the name of the series, the values "
"used for the series and any labels associated with these values can be "
"entered. The data values will generally be entered as references to cells on"
" a worksheet which will allow the plots to be automatically altered when the"
" values in the worksheet change. The series may also have one or more "
"<guilabel>Error</guilabel> tabs in which error values can be associated to "
"the data value of each element in the series."
msgstr ""
"Varje diagram innehåller en eller flera ”serier” som grupperar datavärden. "
"Varje serie har flera egenskaper. På fliken <guilabel>Stil</guilabel> "
"ställer du in utseendet på linjer och punktmarkörer, eller på fyllning och "
"kontur. På fliken <guilabel>Data</guilabel> anger du seriens namn, värden "
"och eventuella etiketter. Värden anges vanligen som referenser till celler i"
" ett kalkylblad, så att diagrammet uppdateras automatiskt när cellerna "
"ändras. Serien kan också ha en eller flera flikar <guilabel>Fel</guilabel>, "
"där du kopplar felvärden till varje datapunkt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4359
msgid "Series line style"
msgstr "Linjestil för en dataserie"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4361
msgid ""
"Series in line plots, in some radar plots and in scatter plots will have a "
"style tab in which the graphical style of the lines and point markers can be"
" established."
msgstr ""
"Serier i linjediagram, vissa radardiagram och spridningsdiagram har en "
"stilflik där du ställer in linjernas utseende och punktmarkörer."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4368
msgid "The configurable properties of a line style."
msgstr "Egenskaper som kan ställas in för en linjestil."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4376
msgid ""
"This screenshot depicts the properties of a line style which can be "
"configured."
msgstr ""
"Skärmbilden visar vilka egenskaper för en linjestil som kan ställas in."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4382
msgid ""
"The properties of a single value data series include an optional name, a "
"required list of values and an optional list of labels. The name, in this "
"case, is a reference to cell D7 in the first worksheet. The values are the "
"contents of the cells in the range E7:I7. The labels are the contents of the"
" cells in the range E6:I6. Note that there are as many cells in the labels "
"range as in the values range."
msgstr ""
"Egenskaperna för en dataserie med enstaka värden omfattar ett valfritt namn,"
" en obligatorisk värdelista och en valfri etikettlista. Här är namnet en "
"referens till cell D7 i det första kalkylbladet. Värdena hämtas från "
"cellerna E7:I7 och etiketterna från E6:I6. Antalet celler i etikettområdet "
"är samma som i värdeområdet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4397
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Line</guilabel> properties include the line color and size. "
"The color can be altered in the standard way using the drop down color "
"chooser. The width of the line can be changed with the spin box. A line size"
" of '-1' means that the line will not be plotted."
msgstr ""
"Under <guilabel>Linje</guilabel> ställer du in linjens färg och tjocklek. "
"Välj färg med rullgardinsknappen och ändra tjockleken med sifferfältets "
"pilar. Värdet ’-1’ innebär att linjen inte ritas."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4405
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Marker</guilabel> properties determine the style of the "
"graphical symbol which will be plotted for each data value. The first drop "
"down box allows the user to choose between a number of different symbols. "
"The blank symbol indicates that no symbol will be plotted where the data "
"value would be. Each shape will have a fill color, and an outline with both "
"a color and a size. The colors can be changed by clicking on the drop down "
"box and picking one of the given colors or using the color picker to select "
"a new color. The size of the outline can be altered by clicking in the text "
"area and editing the value or by using the spin arrows to increase or "
"decrease the size."
msgstr ""
"Under <guilabel>Markör</guilabel> väljer du vilken symbol som ska visas vid "
"varje datavärde. I den första rullgardinsmenyn väljer du symbol. En tom "
"symbol innebär att ingen symbol visas. Varje form har en fyllningsfärg och "
"en kontur med egen färg och storlek. Ändra färg med rullgardinsmenyn eller "
"färgväljaren. Ändra konturens storlek genom att skriva ett nytt värde i "
"textfältet eller använda pilarna."
